PROJECT REPORT
VEHICLE RENTAL SYSTEM
1. ABSTRACT

The Vehicle Rental System is a Java-based console application designed to manage vehicles, customers, rentals, returns, billing, and rental history.

The project is developed using Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts such as classes, objects, constructors, inheritance, method overriding, polymorphism, composition, and collections. It also uses file handling to save and load data from text files.

The system provides a simple menu-driven interface that allows users to add, display, search, and remove vehicles, manage customers, rent and return vehicles, calculate rental bills, and maintain rental history.

2. INTRODUCTION

Vehicle rental businesses need to maintain information about vehicles, customers, rental duration, availability, billing, and rental history.

The Vehicle Rental System provides a simple computerized solution for managing these operations. The application is developed in Java and uses different classes to represent vehicles, customers, and rentals.

The system supports different types of vehicles, such as cars and bikes, using inheritance and polymorphism. Data can also be stored in text files so that information can be loaded when the application starts and saved when required.

